  "description": "AROVOT crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C150 H140 Hg2 N18 Nd12 O6 Se24 2+,2(C18 H15 Hg1 Se3 1-),2.8(C5 H5 N1). From the CIF bond table, Hg4 (Hg) has 0 O neighbors; Hg4A (Hg) has 0 O neighbors; Hg1 (Hg) has 0 O neighbors; Nd1 (Nd) has 4 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 1 O neighbors; Nd3 (Nd) has 2 O neighbors; Nd4 (Nd) has 2 O neighbors; Nd5 (Nd) has 2 O neighbors; Nd6 (Nd) has 1 O neighbors; Hg1A (Hg) has 0 O neighbors; Nd1A (Nd) has 4 O neighbors; Nd2A (Nd) has 1 O neighbors; Nd3A (Nd) has 2 O neighbors; Nd4A (Nd) has 2 O neighbors; Nd5A (Nd) has 2 O neighbors; Nd6A (Nd) has 1 O neighbors; Hg2? (Hg) has 0 O neighbors; Hg3? (Hg) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 29 pairs, 7 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.675-3.966 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 99.18-117.66°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C200H184Hg4N20.8Nd12O6Se30.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
